2. **`connect_pins()`** –  
   `connect_pins("#PWR1", "1", "SW1", "A")`  
   (uses pin 1 of the GND symbol – the only pin – to pin A of the switch).

3. **`write_out_all_wires()`** – writes the single wire into the schematic file.

**Why this layout is optimal**

- The switch sits near the centre, so the schematic remains balanced.  
- Rotating the switch to 90° aligns its common pin horizontally, making the wire to ground a straight vertical line.  
- The GND symbol is placed just below, ensuring the wire is short and the ground reference is visible.  
- No extra components introduce unnecessary clutter.  

